  "chapter": 9,
  "sortOrder": 46009,
  "verseCount": 27,
  "aliases": [
    "1 Cor",
    "1Cor",
    "1 Co",
    "1Co"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Am I not an apostle? am I not free? have I not seen Jesus Christ our Lord? are not ye my work in the Lord?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "If I be not an apostle unto others, yet doubtless I am to you: for the seal of mine apostleship are ye in the Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Mine answer to them that do examine me is this,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Have we not power to eat and to drink?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Have we not power to lead about a sister, a wife, as well as other apostles, and as the brethren of the Lord, and Cephas?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Or I only and Barnabas, have not we power to forbear working?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Who goeth a warfare any time at his own charges? who planteth a vineyard, and eateth not of the fruit thereof? or who feedeth a flock, and eateth not of the milk of the flock?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Say I these things as a man? or saith not the law the same also?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For it is written in the law of Moses, Thou shalt not muzzle the mouth of the ox that treadeth out the corn. Doth God take care for oxen?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Or saith he it altogether for our sakes? For our sakes, no doubt, this is written: that he that ploweth should plow in hope; and that he that thresheth in hope should be partaker of his hope.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "If we have sown unto you spiritual things, is it a great thing if we shall reap your carnal things?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "If others be partakers of this power over you, are not we rather? Nevertheless we have not used this power; but suffer all things, lest we should hinder the gospel of Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Do ye not know that they which minister about holy things live of the things of the temple? and they which wait at the altar are partakers with the altar?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Even so hath the Lord ordained that they which preach the gospel should live of the gospel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "But I have used none of these things: neither have I written these things, that it should be so done unto me: for it were better for me to die, than that any man should make my glorying void.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "For though I preach the gospel, I have nothing to glory of: for necessity is laid upon me; yea, woe is unto me, if I preach not the gospel!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "For if I do this thing willingly, I have a reward: but if against my will, a dispensation of the gospel is committed unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "What is my reward then? Verily that, when I preach the gospel, I may make the gospel of Christ without charge, that I abuse not my power in the gospel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "For though I be free from all men, yet have I made myself servant unto all, that I might gain the more.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "And unto the Jews I became as a Jew, that I might gain the Jews; to them that are under the law, as under the law, that I might gain them that are under the law;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "To them that are without law, as without law, (being not without law to God, but under the law to Christ,) that I might gain them that are without law.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "To the weak became I as weak, that I might gain the weak: I am made all things to all men, that I might by all means save some.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "And this I do for the gospel’s sake, that I might be partaker thereof with you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Know ye not that they which run in a race run all, but one receiveth the prize? So run, that ye may obtain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "And every man that striveth for the mastery is temperate in all things. Now they do it to obtain a corruptible crown; but we an incorruptible.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "I therefore so run, not as uncertainly; so fight I, not as one that beateth the air:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "But I keep under my body, and bring it into subjection: lest that by any means, when I have preached to others, I myself should be a castaway.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "1 Corinthians 9:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:1-corinthians:9:27"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
